	"description": [
		"Often controversial, U.S.-Latin American relations occupy a special place in the foreign policy of the United States. Students compare differing views of political issues of importance to both regions and explore the emergence of U.S. power, interventionism, cooperation, revolution, collective security, the transition to democracy and the influence of economic factors on the relationship between Latin America and the U.S. Offered in alternate years."
